{"title":"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MegaMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MegaMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Educated_Guess_and_Engineer&#39;s_Induction_(Fake_solve))\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Educated Guess and Engineer's Induction (Fake solve))</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71aad8bf13931d45ebf9597825aaf2a6d4a08fa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13!}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"39\" /> is a perfect square can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca9bbc9455cf09e661950ec6fd234b8e9c41072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^a3^b5^c7^d11^e13^f,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3a6878fef6ec913f2941426896391fcff07f3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d,e,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> are positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/4887250a63a12f304251ecc9bab9ee6a765ae0cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d+e+f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MegaMath\">Video Solution by MegaMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MegaMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EqLTyGanr4s&amp;t=136s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EqLTyGanr4s&amp;t=136s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651c6746e6615c978821ad9350dab20e297166d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> as a prime factorization, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba8dff5a9c8813ceaa6a5f973dab7ce4e0d9bd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10}\\cdot3^5\\cdot5^2\\cdot7\\cdot11\\cdot13.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"174\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>For the fraction to be a square, it needs each prime to be an even power. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> must contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/533459dcd20bf2900528340fe3dd522ceb114b70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\cdot11\\cdot13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> can contain any even power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b2422eb1e019642032c00b0c5d5982903fe45d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />, any odd power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1e08b95f20dbf79d830d08ac7f3f6a90e2f072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{5}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and any even power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b1820deed69da37d7cffb93dec8d3ff6c0c95ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. The sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4ccc90f7efd1401ee198039f6429107165a6190.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2^0+2^2+2^4+2^6+2^8+2^{10})(3^1+3^3+3^5)(5^0+5^2)(7^1)(11^1)(13^1) =\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/481b4da7a9ae43b212a4ef162e4c6ddbffa22c8f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1365\\cdot273\\cdot26\\cdot7\\cdot11\\cdot13 = 2\\cdot3^2\\cdot5\\cdot7^3\\cdot11\\cdot13^4.\\]\" width=\"380\" height=\"15\" /> Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c78b5db3ab280f362a9ba1163fd11cf2f20a9f9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+1+3+1+4=\\boxed{012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"230\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~chem1kall\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651c6746e6615c978821ad9350dab20e297166d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4fa2d9c99a0e0933621bbe3bce45e83ca17b48f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{10} \\cdot 3^5 \\cdot 5^2 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13.\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"15\" />\nTo get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71aad8bf13931d45ebf9597825aaf2a6d4a08fa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13!}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"39\" /> a perfect square, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1bafb6c1d5561bae41f152f374737f22072cfa7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 2^{2x} \\cdot 3^{1 + 2y} \\cdot 5^{2z} \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"241\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f921b750b7a8ea17c5467928a5d73170520abb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\left\\{ 0, 1, \\cdots , 5 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8982a2b3edfe2cec5302d4118a42d001684b8e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\in \\left\\{ 0, 1, 2 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95fba813461404b127ffba650a4b09511f03f530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z \\in \\left\\{ 0, 1 \\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, the sum of all feasible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14bda995f053ac94ad45d46fbb0b6cdbb1c9aa3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{x=0}^5 \\sum_{y=0}^2 \\sum_{z=0}^1 2^{2x} \\cdot 3^{1 + 2y} \\cdot 5^{2z} \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13 &amp; = \\left( \\sum_{x=0}^5 2^{2x} \\right) \\left( \\sum_{y=0}^2 3^{1 + 2y} \\right) \\left( \\sum_{z=0}^1 5^{2z} \\right) 7 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13 \\\\ &amp; = \\frac{4^6 - 1}{4-1} \\cdot \\frac{3 \\cdot \\left( 9^3 - 1 \\right)}{9 - 1} \\cdot \\frac{25^2  - 1}{25 - 1} \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13 \\\\ &amp;  = 2 \\cdot 3^2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7^3 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13^4 . \\end{align*}\" width=\"647\" height=\"124\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/405532468816d801d8ff96b59ea78e85338ac466.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 1 + 2 + 1 + 3 + 1 + 4 &amp; = \\boxed{012} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"230\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Educated_Guess_and_Engineer.27s_Induction_.28Fake_solve.29.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Educated_Guess_and_Engineer's_Induction_(Fake_solve))\">Solution 3 (Educated Guess and Engineer's Induction (Fake solve))</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Educated Guess and Engineer&#39;s Induction (Fake solve))\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Try smaller cases. There is clearly only one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> that makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9ce017ae3444360ba7c38942226c3db29e8426e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2!}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"39\" /> a square, and this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3eaf8047a3f5bebfc5c43e27123a15a44d7540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. Here, the sum of the exponents in the prime factorization is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Furthermore, the only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> that makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0eea6fd1845260c45726ddb38b6ff169e75f19a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3!}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"39\" /> a square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/8/0a8ed64229e70927df1b7bbe781b32f1c1803efd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 6 = 2^13^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />, and the sum of the exponents is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> here. Trying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c511381af18b2d60b28c9a2690d8208d8931fda2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/31679fa804f9f446682af96f7552cbd5f0d5d140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5!}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"39\" />, the sums of the exponents are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Based on this, we (incorrectly!) conclude that, when we are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad1c03293dd9678d78f415846c694fb95c0b657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n!}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"38\" />, the desired sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. The problem gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71aad8bf13931d45ebf9597825aaf2a6d4a08fa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13!}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"39\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb187a728e0713b5fa11b529a643281655356df8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13-1 = \\boxed{012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>-InsetIowa9\n</p><p>However...\n</p><p>The induction fails starting at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/1819f547a53f667e1a44a49ba2bec08c28d7f222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 9$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />&#160;!\nThe actual answers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> for small <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89af13630a5a7a2f9721495857c024925b600e0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 7, 7, 8, 11, 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"235\" height=\"17\" />\nIn general, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/350af858ffbbb2ba691d8824b3d05c4d0d832c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p) = f(p-1)+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" /> if p is prime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/613290dc19180c7cfadb573f9e79e8e1bbbe32ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4,6,8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" /> are \"lucky\", and the pattern breaks down after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4f171162b090bab7ce5dfa1c58715850530ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>-\"fake\"  warning by oinava\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>I also somewhat try to explain how the formula for sum of the divisors works, not sure I succeeded. Was 3 AM lol.\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MUYC2fBF2U4&amp;list=PL-27w0UNlunz8cLtB66rbjofQ7ubEkkyB&amp;index=4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MUYC2fBF2U4&amp;list=PL-27w0UNlunz8cLtB66rbjofQ7ubEkkyB&amp;index=4</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I\" title=\"2023 AIME I\">2023 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2023\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2023 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"